      "content": "1|**Submitted by:** [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]]  \n2|**Tier:** Tier 1  \n3|**Recommended Level:** 3  \n4|**Expected Length:** One-shot, approximately 3-4 hours  \n5|**Tone:** Haunted ruin investigation, mercenary recovery job, old colonial oaths  \n6|**Location:** [[The Outback]] / Shrine of the Oathsworn Knights\n7|\n8|### Public Notice\n9|\n10|> **THC SEEKS LICENSED ADVENTURERS AFTER HIGHBLADE KNIGHTS VANISH IN THE OUTBACK**\n11|\n12|The [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]] seeks licensed adventurers for an urgent recovery and containment contract beyond the city roads of [[Stickyickistan]]. Recent ground collapse in [[The Outback]] has exposed the buried Shrine of the Oathsworn Knights, an old Highblade military shrine believed to date back to the early expansion campaigns before the modern city-state was fully settled.\n13|\n14|The site lies past reliable patrol routes, where old battlefields, arcane-warped wilderness, and Can we mforgotten ruins make ordinary travel unsafe. Caravan hands and prospectors passing near the collapse have reported voices beneath the stone, cold lights moving after sundown, and the sound of armored feet marching where no living patrol has been posted.\n15|\n16|**Sir Emil Corvian**, **Sir Petros Valescu**, and **Squire Joseph Wrenhollow** were dispatched from the Coalition to secure the location, assess any surviving military relics, and determine whether the shrine poses a threat to Tribunal holdings or nearby settlements. No report has been received, and no signal flare has been sighted.\n17|\n18|Applicants should be prepared for unstable ruins, old wards, oathbound dead, and the possibility of arcanite interference affecting magic, navigation, or communications. This is a player-facing recovery contract, not a salvage free-for-all. Any Highblade arms, banners, records, or sealed relics recovered from the shrine are to be declared to the Coalition quartermaster for review.\n19|\n20|Once a party is formed, report to the THC contract desk at [[Highblade Tower]] on [[Nevercough Island]], or to the licensed guildhall officer holding this notice, for travel papers, last-known-route details, and hazard pay terms.\n21|\n22|The Coalition offers payment to capable adventurers who can reach the shrine, determine the fate of the missing patrol, recover survivors if possible, and ensure that whatever still keeps watch beneath the ruins does not wander back toward Stickyickistan.\n23|\n24|## Rewards\n25|\n26|- **Up to 600 XP each** for completing the adventure.\n27|- **225 gp each** from the [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]] for investigating the shrine and resolving the disturbance.\n28|- Gratitude, formal commendation, or future contract preference from the [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]].\n29|- Possible future favor with House Highblade contacts for those who handle oathbound remains and military relics with discretion.\n30|- The opportunity to claim approved salvage, monster components, and non-restricted relics after Coalition review.\n31|- Possible bonus XP for rescuing missing personnel, preserving important records, preventing restless spirits from spreading beyond the site, or resolving the matter without needless damage to the shrine.\n32|",
